Z||000000||turbo86se||01-18-2000||11:12 AM||||<BR>Hi TOM, I'm responding to your post about the three 88's going to the crusher. I should have thought about this earlier, but if you are going back to the junk yard anytime soon, could you look into whether or not the automatic 88 has a computer? My computer on my 88 automatic is going bad (hard to start). <BR>The service numbers are: 1227748.  I've got a spare I keep with me just in case the original one dies, but the car won't shift into overdrive! Thanks for your help!   -joel||||reg||5
Z||000001||TOM||01-18-2000||07:46 PM||||I will have a look see||||reg||1
Z||000002||terryk||01-19-2000||11:46 PM||||turbo86se,<P>Are you using an automatic transmission prom? <P>Actually, most manual trans proms will lock the TCC all of the time so that might not be it.<P>87 and 88 4-bangers use the same ECM.||||reg||1
Z||000003||turbo86se||01-20-2000||12:11 AM||||Terryk, I am using the stock computer now, but I've got a back-up from another Fiero (I have no idea what year), the service numbers match. I haven't had to use it yet, knock on wood. <BR>Maybe this is related, but I've noticed the car starts fine with half a tank or less, but when I fill it up, or try to start with a near full tank, it fails! The fuel pump and filter are brand-new. Does this sound familiar?  My trustworthy mechanic says it's the computer, while I tried starting it, he looked somewhere down the throttle body and couldn't see a spark? That could be wrong on my part. <BR>Any suggestions?||||reg||1
Z||000004||cobra427||01-20-2000||02:23 AM||||turbo86se, if you give me the production ECM # (which will start with the #'s 160.....)maybe I can give you the year of the ECM. Only 87,88 start with 161.....# (only 1 in 87 and 2 in 88). Just to double check the ECM,give me the "production broadcast code" as well.Example:-CLM or ANBP .||||reg||1
Z||000005||cobra427||01-20-2000||07:48 PM||||turbo86se.<BR>I got your E=Mail and here is what i come up with.  It is used in either a 87-88 L-4 engine/5-speed. The only difference that i could see was that the 87 has a different<BR>(service calibrator[prom])#-16143453 as opposed to the 88, which has the 16122664(sevice calabrator [prom]). All the other #'s match for the 87-88 L-4 5/spd models. Esentually the same ECM. Hope this has helped.   (Taken from 22P manual& other info.)<p>[This message has been edited by cobra427 (edited 01-20-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000006||turbo86se||01-21-2000||02:18 PM||||Cobra427, you're right about where the computer came from! Now that I think about it, my mechanic does have a stripped 87 coupe 5-spd. That must be where the computer came from! Thanks!||||reg||10
